    "reasoning": "Fifteen answers are confirmed by their own captured worked solutions. q-65402 uses sec²x−tan²x=1. q-120652 uses tan²x/sec²x=sin²x, giving 2sin²x−1=1−2cos²x. q-23853 is (sec²x−tan²x)²=1. q-43292 simplifies to tan²θ(sec²θ−1)=tan⁴θ. q-120807 has denominator tan²x(sec²x−tan²x)+1=sec²x, giving cos²x. q-120666 reduces to tan²θ−1=sec²θ−2. These identities hold on the original expressions' domains. q-6828 contains a substantive source error: real t≠0 implies t²>0, so x>5, not merely x≠5. MA's equation and option 0 also include the unattainable branch x<5; no offered choice describes the complete parametrized curve. q-15752 and q-102682 follow by isolating sine and cosine and adding their squares. q-106032 uses equal amplitudes 1/2, giving radius 1/2. q-79192 and q-79170 have the required centers and radii; at θ=0 they start at the rightmost point with upward velocity, hence traverse counterclockwise once. q-106293 shows the closed second-quadrant arc, requiring θ∈[π/2,π]. q-79221 has center (−2,−3) and radius 3. q-84108 eliminates t to give y=−x²/3, passing through (−3,−3). q-106412 eliminates t to give y=−x²/2, matching the vertex and (4,−8). No earlier submitted answer or captured grade was supplied; confirmation rests on the quoted worked solutions.",
